The Co-op said it did not recognize the criticism and said its probate advi=
sers were highly engaged.

Resentment of workers=E2=80=99 treatment is already translating into policy=
, a break from the sluggishness of most technology regulations. Across the =
Atlantic and the continental United States, Governor Gavin Newsom of Califo=
rnia signed laws into effect last week that prohibit certain types of workp=
lace surveillance.

California=E2=80=99s laws aim to target workplace surveillance measures lik=
e heat maps that track employees=E2=80=99 movements, including how long the=
y spend in the bathroom, or having their emotional states monitored. Amazon=
 warehouse workers have previously complained about being timed on their ba=
throom breaks, for example. And at Kaiser Permanente, a California hospital=
 chain, nurses have said automated systems rated their tone of voice in pat=
ient interactions.

