yle=3D"font-family:Georgia, serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1;text-align:l=
eft;color:#000000;"><h2 style=3D"margin: 0; font-size: 24px; color: #121212=
;">Elon Musk=E2=80=99s orbital ownership</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Elon Musk=E2=80=99s SpaceX is the single l=
argest satellite operator in the world, larger than any government space bu=
reau. The life-threatening consequences of that dominance and centralizatio=
n of power are on full display. One man is in charge of global, vital infra=
structure, which is thumbing the scales in the war on Ukraine.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">SpaceX=E2=80=99s internet service was thro=
ttled in Ukraine amid a series of devastating attacks by Russia last week, =
leaving the country extremely vulnerable. The US government controls StarSh=
ield, the satellite internet service produced by SpaceXSI for the Pentagon,=
 which is what Ukraine relies on. Objects moving faster than 100 mph (160.9=
 km/h) =E2=80=93 drones, the centerpiece of Ukraine=E2=80=99s counteroffens=
ive =E2=80=93 lost connectivity. The sudden restrictions Tuesday evening le=
d to <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLME=
mFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEB-ac_e6ZWOBuq0B2fiARjlHje5VY-Kk0A0dg8E-4f=
QzvgSBk6qddgq28dNUXECQla3vZhM9v-clxL4y1TDCohMir_xQcGwGCBEIu9LmF0Z_PVX3byYEc=
2vQMv5P930KlnzcEBUtUjI9LK1Wh2aeLmaocr7g-DJqiKCnZ47VZy8WJa_Rme25B7dPweBeZH_z=
Zx4ZXAt3_8J10HwYyWquPgsS1mZilQzzjXe8_Xpi2P2yVQkgQg6Yt8Q2u5dFKnBEU1Rl0MqizI4=
fdF5m1u7Hdl1/4v1/lNPqQ1e7RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h20/h001.EdU33bOp7olvweTgC8OsebM4nw=
ncmrGdgACCP9m3lR8" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the failure of several Ukraini=
an combat missions</a>. Russian drones fly at nearly 200 mph (328.9 km/h), =
so Ukrainian interceptor drones can=E2=80=99t catch them without Starlink, =
and no alternative is as yet viable. In response, Ukrainian president Volod=
ymyr Zelensky warned =E2=80=9Cpeople will die.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The cutoff comes alongside Donald Trump=E2=
=80=99s mercurial souring on Ukraine. Pressured domestically by the high pr=
ice of diesel and upcoming midterm elections, the US president has eased sa=
nctions on Russia, and Zelensky has said US intelligence agencies on severa=
l occasions in recent days didn=E2=80=99t warn Ukraine of incoming missile =
attacks, as they usually do. Musk has denied his own involvement in StarShi=
eld=E2=80=99s malfunctioning, writing, =E2=80=9CThis is not under SpaceX co=
ntrol.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.thegua=
rdian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR4TlkV015Ok9576v5vLffIyLQ03kQo4nLTz=
VZabT20u173BsO13NHVmUACceQIAZnXW4WegFECOqPZDz1I9JYtVAWNiyKmj4TfTCl43bZWukeA=
UjmD7LT8yAdG2x6YqO3EO5edNKW_KufOUVtuCDJ7vBw0zhRQc8Xh7Im8qWIVG5sQbOSg6TgUS4X=
gRilWwLbFswQ0wmZv-8_f_W9SifNIVbXYJgtngg37S0xC7u1-9W-Lg3F28MVN8NBX125JF3heew=
E-HtG9AO156-ftmUYG_ncLOETnpd9K6j73G1xRei/4v1/lNPqQ1e7RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h21/h00=
1.PT38UM_CGJwMOAtSmEtTOq5njVScKXThqjTgyiDGsOo" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Re=
uters</a> reported that the request to throttle the service in Ukraine came=
 from the White House. Responding to the claim, Trump said: =E2=80=9CI don=
=E2=80=99t know if it was anybody because it wasn=E2=80=99t me, and I don=
=E2=80=99t think it was Elon. And from what I understand, it=E2=80=99s the =
same as it=E2=80=99s always been.=E2=80=9D US secretary of state Marco Rubi=
o said =E2=80=9Cno one at the White House ordered anyone to slow down the i=
nternet.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Read more: <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
CSneHEB-ac_e6ZWOBuq0B2fiARjlLuTdAtjs4PgMKQMDjx64PNvIP1H1iHpVmvsCpZOB5gAisk0=
zQfFWMHD02WgL6fMM2z6QTnvkMh5ukP-hOpBZLeyT21IYzyeR3wr4DvQoSL8J41jILtyKQaCiS7=
fjLYuG38PffEqKRb4M2sJeVX_KvFY1G_iOz9GShj3HEZ2Ff_HgRnaoXmaqmD6T9aSuS20mDPfB9=
dNnOmGEJLo1QVdbyD1PRu2DHsaxxb9p18ZCUJQ/4v1/lNPqQ1e7RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h22/h001.=
1ocNeGfN-yRL-H_E2bN7gbVujt1VyZrT72trSUW5Q8w" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">What=
 is Starshield, SpaceX=E2=80=99s military-grade Starlink system, and how wi=
ll its restriction affect Ukraine?</a></strong></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Musk=E2=80=99s denial has been met with sk=
epticism given his close ties with the administration. It is impossible to =
disentangle him and SpaceX from the Trump administration. He has realigned =
himself with the White House in recent months, patching up his explosive fe=
ud with the president from a year ago and appearing with Trump at major eve=
nts. Musk has been appointed to a Pentagon commission on the future of war =
and has given hundreds of millions of dollars to conservative Republican ca=
ndidates.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Musk has also personally ordered the restr=
iction of Starlink service in Ukraine before. In 2022, SpaceX cut off Starl=
ink =E2=80=93 not StarShield =E2=80=93 service during a Ukrainian counterof=
fensive in the regions of Kherson and Donetsk. He refused Ukraine=E2=80=99s=
 request to extend connectivity to Crimea the same year.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">One tech tycoon=E2=80=99s political leanin=
gs are determining the tides of war between two sovereign nations. Musk=E2=
=80=99s alliance with the White House implicates him in the pressure campai=
gn against Ukraine to end the war with Russia, likely via surrender.</p>
