<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In recent weeks, notable musicians have co=
nfronted the growing presence of AI-generated music, saying they are open t=
o it but wary, even boosters like the singer and producer Grimes, former pa=
ramour of Musk and mother to three of his 14 children.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Fans, by contrast, are voting with million=
s of streams against artifice in music. Songs and albums harkening back to =
analog instrumentation are dominating the Billboard charts, no futurism wan=
ted.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Both A$AP Rocky, rapper and partner to Rih=
anna, and Grimes took the same position: I accept AI-generated music, but I=
 don=E2=80=99t make it.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CI prefer to do things myself, pra=
ctically,=E2=80=9D A$AP Rocky told <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theg=
uardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR7OoWW5y58_Ro4VGat10mdCIIprngWZpU=
QQULRBBO5eKhCSJ29m9dEu5SW1FlbhgLiVH52usU8gJZ3LxH5duT7lsiBHvw0e4c8PdJV0CzzKN=
jUrW0DYNU2VKG33HnliRChJ-EIdjC50Yj7R3Q4YUazvuHhk0Z0KDoq57RGIxs0BD17aTZKo1lZj=
WqLFrrIHyu8u9GYfB1_upjr-_-1euQQBWRbDEBurbP0HaOQNQu3B015spe6FsjNcOTbjikSqxMQ=
/4v1/lNPqQ1e7RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h23/h001.z7kHFTMH_AiI4GmBkX1CRRDMbqTtjmv4vw01RP=
a_lzA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Billboard</a>. =E2=80=9CIf somebody does a=
 totally AI-generated song where all they did was prompt something, then I =
think that=E2=80=99s their thing. But who am I to say what=E2=80=99s standa=
rd and what=E2=80=99s not? I=E2=80=99m just doing me out here, and I=E2=80=
=99m doing my music practically =E2=80=93 the right way.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Grimes, one of my own favorite musicians, =
has begun promoting her first new album in six years, Psy Opera, which she =
described to <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.=
Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRy9hm6avC_yoBgCjrxdkr9wDHLOfkb0KwhfXBqHTEfr8KLDRHYuK1O6=
GLz6rhY3pb025iCi_Om8Nn4lnTxk6MvuxX4tRJ2xRdsi3lTdk5Z6aC0ib0ZO53TKysoXKRtC_g1=
D5LO_ukSQ1XBDW_mmHOaBzCu9k7DvRlhbWchuZ4aR4lAB1u9wFG4A4zD_7s31vPZomVxNEwxLp6=
_AvIal553KUTZ8R7q4dc52s5EpKxeSQSpexTh_sBkjo4gpwcHDodw/4v1/lNPqQ1e7RzeR8J-An=
uL-eQ/h24/h001.NXvJ9Kw6bUrS-WTQTosCeiLS7Di0XBAPBVo-z8NHoig" style=3D"color:=
 #0077B6;">The Paris Review</a> as capturing the =E2=80=9Cemotion of being =
thrust into the future=E2=80=9D. <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.thegua=
rdian.com/ss/c/u001.zFrJr-OAD6MUXPGxMNJG7EqeHnbBO97Dx2jnV0GWxHhu5rBWj1DTr26=
S6825b075FNy2KgccyNADTsVifGO5dxTOu86cm_XFAFIMlq9e7ugVEEH7nAGzR3ZOt6NC5xJx74=
g8baKUz7HWKWn18J_pA5jPA1QUn0e8iAKW55W2Kdcu-W-267yPUnbnQhtY_k7A4qGU4WzQiVKw3=
y9QZU0gVP0FsNmTy_o1EGHb4PRObD-U-6g9QxiCG6AmpugPchCYr8eYuC4ci0YW00rYqoOgi8Hl=
vscp7ixE8Q-QQlCTbhZb-u2Q-c19asEwj8E3oRUlrCO5--4bkIE1cldgcz1zTQ/4v1/lNPqQ1e7=
RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h25/h001.adPEE5R4Oc-7973QSlA5MC68gky4peACQk508-rw0FY" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">Stereogum</a> described the album as =E2=80=9CAI-inspi=
red but not AI-generated=E2=80=9D, citing Grimes=E2=80=99 own insistence th=
at her team of 70 be credited rather than reduced to machines.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Grimes offered a free license of her own v=
oice to AI enthusiasts to make what they would three years ago. That she de=
clined to generate her own music indicates that, even to a futurist like he=
r, AI-generated music is lacking, similar to Rocky=E2=80=99s stance.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">I have also found myself listening to an A=
I-generated song, Bomboclat Wallahi, brought to my attention via <a href=3D=
"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR9N=
JKsxYgqJheqAQJ2aJHuC11qp-iPVr_SDV8wWYcObEaJYbIm50mOw01lrinaI4WgUZF2Q0msSTx6=
peOEGz22kenael2e7WaIGZwT-pm678kDS97DqrGMfWv_OjMIVz_QHDCEmOe55yJYO5VVaZ9imFf=
oBUuMA97nlkT3izup16fK9ZdqQN3xZphIFIvX1DN-2SJpNLdgrQIh20i0apTVQMHXKxvbo1U3Us=
iMOno1p9vZrc5Hgzgies6YWV3JVGDSFwgUB2J3-aTxf-C0eup4z_SzcSERgmNrOtZ8txLLK_/4v=
1/lNPqQ1e7RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h26/h001.YTj72Np1LkYm7O_spFZQP2sTPdmIb7zplHVHXpuq-=
Pg" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">frenetic</a>, overstimulating <a href=3D"http=
s://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR9NJKsxY=
gqJheqAQJ2aJHuAghlZevZ8EQ_IDTpAg_Al5w-NEkQDNweJYLp2MrhNuFm-GVehLta4ONlc5sYK=
GGLqAv5nP3JejyynjgJRLRsDNiwlQ1_Led5g5F_s8xzMxULzvAT0d4esdBDaAogvXvqXuCyVTgm=
Ztv_-vOQ9bo9aAVl1zcKpGx0Wf6k54DumKCB8uPGHZbPNYPY3rwPccJQlu6WfItHn9kxEPQu-bk=
L6cs_Q2kRsbFdoLNc2gS52B7zeEMTs0GuhaAYE7kJL7ngqIG5-5HeGMlqrGjprLdcd_/4v1/lNP=
qQ1e7RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h27/h001.knDbIW7GZz7W5MdV-tP22kr_9tUFv9iEBLauLOKnruA" s=
tyle=3D"color: #0077B6;">videos</a> on Instagram. Despite the song=E2=80=99=
s comical sonic maximalism, it lacks any staying power. Listening to it the=
 day after I first heard it left no impression, similar to the way low-qual=
ity food leaves me hungry again just a few hours after eating. =E2=80=9CSlo=
p=E2=80=9D is still the best word to describe AI-made content.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In contrast to artists=E2=80=99 nuanced st=
ances, fans are making their position on tech-made music clear: They don=E2=
=80=99t want it. <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u=
001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR7OoWW5y58_Ro4VGat10mdCt1BvTVR0i-Ezd2TcxjlM3QAyWbYG=
LFhDBq5P2OzJUEbdyG6nFmRSWXpxzQh2tKh3bV0XrsRCJ--MKfUpl8Gp1NQt4NSgwh00Ku8Ll6Z=
5OlxCZuFzedkLlYCIqy3lN1fjZBpusOxs6xw-N5WJeUFuRQ5zv_SFDUDvL1pZ63AMbkQ/4v1/lN=
PqQ1e7RzeR8J-AnuL-eQ/h28/h001.AAQ8Se_YGyJXSa_ZL_oxeK3aMiqPD_Xtv6ooMd9P7l4" =
style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Billboard=E2=80=99s charts</a> of the most popula=
r albums and charts of the past week showcase a preference for music withou=
t obvious modification. Songs and albums that feature a simple voice-and-gu=
itar arrangement are dominating. On the Top 200 album charts, most of the T=
op 10 albums foreground a singer over analog instrumentation =E2=80=93 Oliv=
ia Rodrigo=E2=80=99s you seem pretty sad for a girl so in love, Ella Langle=
y=E2=80=99s Dandelion, Olivia Dean=E2=80=99s The Art of Loving, Taylor Swif=
t=E2=80=99s The Life of a Showgirl, Noah Kahan=E2=80=99s The Great Divide a=
nd Stick Season, and Morgan Wallen=E2=80=99s I=E2=80=99m the Problem. In th=
e Hot 100 singles chart, the top four songs bear the same sonic signatures:=
 Swift=E2=80=99s Patient Zero, Langley=E2=80=99s Choosin=E2=80=99 Texas, St=
ella Lefty=E2=80=99s Boston, Wallen=E2=80=99s Been by Now.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Incredibly, The Beatles=E2=80=99 Rubber So=
ul, released in 1965, also makes an appearance at No 4 on last week=E2=80=
=99s Billboard rankings. Some listeners want to return to a time when produ=
cing music with artificial intelligence wasn=E2=80=99t even an option.</p>
