<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em>My colleague Robert Booth reports from=
 the Hacking Big Tech conference, a Guardian conference in Paris:</em></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">As the Paris Streets erupted with protest =
and violence on Saturday, a parallel radicalism was on display at the Hacki=
ng Big Tech conference organised by the French media organization Mediapart=
 in conjunction with the Guardian. Amid the contributions from experts in m=
ilitary AI and how to fight against datacenters, a theme emerged about how =
people might respond to the tech wave: be more human.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The writer Naomi Klein told the audience t=
hat the technology companies intend AI to be used as an =E2=80=9Ceverything=
 app and also as a truth machine=E2=80=9D. This, she said, was =E2=80=9Cver=
y clearly a fascist idea, to centralise knowledge, to standardise what inte=
lligence is=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">At a rare tech conference not addressed by=
 representatives of tech companies, Klein painted a bleak AI-driven future =
in which there is =E2=80=9Cgoing to be more resource scarcity, there=E2=80=
=99s going to be more people who have no role in the economy and need to be=
 contained and surveilled=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A response was available, she said: =E2=80=
=9CWe decide that we want to be more human.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Humor was another answer. German Salazar, =
a Chilean activist campaigning to save water in his native country in the f=
ace of a wave of AI datacenters, showed how his community had set up a huma=
n chatbot to encourage people to prompt less and save water. The idea was s=
imple: a team, ranging from children to town elders, offered human response=
s to chatbot queries from anywhere in the world for a day. If you want an i=
mage of a dog doing yoga, one of them will paint it for you. Want to know w=
hat love is? A human will tell you it is =E2=80=9Cthe wish of someone else =
to be happy=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There were 2,300 requests for images, 135 =
for dating advice and one for the meaning of life.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Read more: <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
